    "narrative": "The anchor of today\u2019s lineup is undoubtedly **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.87 against Brady Singer. While Singer isn't a pushover, the combination of **Gunnar Henderson** hitting at the top of the order and benefiting from a 14% dynamic platoon advantage makes him our primary engine for Runs and HRs. We are also leaning heavily into the matchup against Mitch Keller; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.73) and **Curtis Mead** (62.15) both see significant score bumps due to Keller\u2019s 4.60 xERA and favorable park factors. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (71.62) and **Heliot Ramos** (69.03) are clear starts, with **Heliot Ramos** specifically benefiting from a high-upside 19% SP skill boost and an excellent park factor at his venue, positioning them to carry the bulk of our offensive production.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Coby Mayo**, who posted a 51.77 score but ultimately missed the cut due to a negative platoon split (R/R) and a crowded middle infield. His exclusion highlights the high floor of our current starters, particularly **Nasim Nunez**, whose 59.10 score is buoyed by a switch-hitting profile that provides flexibility against the Pirates' staff. While **Sam Antonacci** and **Jackson Merrill** were considered for removal due to tougher matchups against Gavin Williams and Shohei Ohtani respectively, their potential for stolen bases remains a critical component of our strategy given the scarcity of that category in our 5x5 format.\n\nWe must monitor the 38% rain risk surrounding **Brayan Rocchio** and **Sam Antonacci** closely; if either game is impacted, we have depth ready to sub in. Furthermore, since all lineups are currently pending, we are projecting based on historical placement. Should **Liam Hicks** or **Drake Baldwin** drop down the order, their efficiency scores\u2014already hovering near the marginal threshold\u2014could crater, necessitating a swift pivot to the bench. We remain cautious of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (59.48) against Luis Castillo, as the park factor and platoon matchup against a high-tier arm make him the most volatile asset in today's active set.",
